@startuml
title M-SH4 - State ownership and trust boundaries (current / SH1 versus SH2+)
left to right direction

package "Current / SH1 - operator user state, one daemon per BoardKey" {
  component "tb-sessiond\nboard executable / composed host library" as daemon
  component "task-board producers / client" as current_board
  database "Board-keyed session records / logs / transcripts\nlogical host state; operator user directory" as current_records
  database "Per-session notice inbox\nboard producers write directly" as current_inbox
  artifact "Private file: global bearer token\nany operator-user process can use it" as token
  daemon --> current_records : host persistence / self-restoring startup
  current_board --> current_inbox : direct writes
  daemon --> current_inbox : deliver only while client attached
  current_board --> token : current authentication
  note bottom of current_records
    Claude PTY / private Codex app-server are owned by daemon process.
    Claude dies on replacement; restore is current behavior, not SH2 recovery.
    File names / retention / full schema: unspecified in spec §1.1 / §2.
    SH1 host-independent local context policy remains fail-closed (§2.3).
  end note
}

package "SH2+ target - activation gates, not current file layout" {
  node "swarma-session-host service account" {
    component "swarma-session-host" as host
    database "Service-private durable metadata / logs\ntranscripts / audit evidence / receipts\ninbox / goal revisions / fences / controller epochs\nparent-child session authority\nowner: host" as state
    artifact "Published host socket directory\nconnect permissions separate from data privacy" as socket
    artifact "Session + execution-scoped capabilities\naudience / actions / expiry / revocation\nissued by host" as caps
  }
  node "worker-<label> account" {
    component "swarma-session-runner" as runner
    component "Claude Code / private Codex app-server" as harness
    artifact "Managed home / native-session lock\ncontinuity binding: home, profile, transcript digest" as home
  }
  component "swarma-dispatcher" as dispatcher
  database "Admission / allocation / execution / cleanup records\nsession-scoped host admission permit\nowner: dispatcher" as execution
  component "swarma-user-manager / swarma-user-launcher\nroot launch / exec.stop boundary" as manager
  database "Root-owned active-generation ledger\nowner: user manager" as generations
  component "Optional board client\norchestrator account / service account" as board
  database "Goal ledger / ancestry / run evidence\ncompletion barrier / outcomes / publication\nowner: board, outside host" as board_state
  component "agent-session-bridge" as bridge
  database "Durable carrier Mailbox\nowner: bridge" as mail
  component "swarma-credential-broker\nauth owner" as broker

  host --> state : durable write before acknowledgement
  host --> caps : issue / revoke / rotate on replacement
  board --> socket : authenticated calls replace direct file APIs
  board --> board_state : optional adapter records
  bridge --> mail : holds mail durably
  bridge --> socket : enqueue into host inbox
  runner --> socket : re-authenticate / reconnect; current epoch
  runner --> harness : owns PTY master / app-server transport
  runner --> home : preserves admitted native continuity
  runner --> broker : execution lease client; no copied auth.json
  host --> generations : check UID / active generation
  manager --> generations : owns privileged ledger
  dispatcher --> execution : owns execution state / capacity claims
  host --> dispatcher : host_start / host_stop (dispatch-op/1)
  dispatcher --> manager : sole privileged start caller / exec.stop / confirmed absence

  note bottom of state
    Agent-writable files are not trusted transcript/audit evidence.
    Closed fence queues without delivery; unknown permits stay owned.
    Unreadable state is closed, never absence.
    Reconcile unknown delivery against intact transcript before reopening:
    matching marker proves applied; confirmed absence permits redelivery;
    unknown approval/control effects never auto-replay (§3.4).
    Exact files, schema versions, retention and migration:
    unspecified in spec §3.1 / §3.4 / §7.
  end note
  note bottom of home
    F-16: cross-account child repository has own .git / configuration / hooks.
    No linked worktree across isolated accounts; same-account board worktrees stay.
    Runner/harness home file ownership and persistent layout:
    unspecified in spec §3.2 / §3.5; not a shared service credential pool.
    Same-machine resume preserves home/profile/runtime/transport,
    transcript digest, exclusive lock, auth and grants.
    Breaking harness semver refuses; resume failure reports resume-failed;
    no automatic fallback (§3.5).
  end note
  note bottom of generations
    R-GEN: fresh random 128-bit generation; restored ledger closes consumers.
    Host keeps highest observed ledger store epoch; lower epoch refuses pending operator reconciliation.
    Reader floor only helps outside restored domain; never proves whole-machine rollback absent.
  end note
  note bottom of broker
    R-REBIND: E-rebind / binding replacement keeps same UID + generation;
    old-binding tombstone; fresh prepare revocation check; never widens.
    R-TIME: authenticated or operator-controlled time source; dispatcher / broker watermarks.
    Clock steps only narrow authority; expiry destruction also needs monotonic elapsed lifetime.
  end note
  note bottom of socket
    Kernel peer UID, server identity, close-on-exec, one role/connection.
    Managed principal = UID + generation; malformed/unreadable/ambiguous/
    retired ledger entry refuses fallback. Legacy token refused on activation.
    Socket basename / capability wire / FD3-compatible runner channel:
    unspecified in spec §3.1 / §7.
  end note
  note bottom of execution
    Controller epoch, execution ID and account generation are distinct.
    Session-scoped permit: logical_session_id; owner session lifecycle authorisation.
    Each start keeps execution_id / controller_epoch / op_id claim and fence.
    Host durable intent and closed fence precede host_start.
    Fence change withdraws or reconciles affected start authority; host failure retains claim / fence.
    Resolve same ambiguous effect / root receipt; never launch twice.
    Fresh authenticated runner channel / current-epoch registration and readiness
    precede delivery (R-START, §3.3).
    R-MAINT keeps standing allocations / identities; deadline bounds attempt.
    Confirmed absence and reconciliation precede mode/state/binary changes.
    Unknown/refused stop defers maintenance; R-MAINT withdraws permit; restart needs fresh owner admission.
    Live authenticated runner re-adoption keeps execution ID;
    new execution gets new ID. Unknown absence cannot release capacity.
    External record file layouts: unspecified in spec §3.2 / §3.3.
  end note
}

note bottom of dispatcher
  R-SESSION: host_stop only by configured host principal for execution under permit.
  Journaled E-stop / exec.stop / confirmed absence; host-requested, distinct from owner cancel.
  host_stop confers no start authority.
  R-FATE: user manager §7 owns process-class fate table beside R-FD3.
  Survival and service-swap affected set require published unit / per-OS evidence.
  Dispatcher supervisor writes fenced by daemon-instance epoch; no live adoption.
  F-13: latest receipt authorises stop; signalling / absence scope is all UID processes.
  R-SVC-EGRESS: host deny-all, including loopback TCP; Unix-socket calls only.
  Readiness needs verified service row / anchor / resolver restriction (user manager §8).
  F-15: authenticated controls / observation / already-authorised stop stay reachable
  while forward admission is closed; unknown records retain claims.
  R-LOCK: no state lock across dispatcher or runner call; durable in-flight marker.
  Late results revalidated under lock; stale results never reopen delivery / admission.
  Detailed host wait/lock graph: M-SH5 / spec §3.4.
end note
